<title>FRANCE: Monep, MATIF open outcry halted after bomb alert.</title>
<headline>Monep, MATIF open outcry halted after bomb alert.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Open outcry trading on the MATIF futures market and trading on the Monep options market was suspended after a bomb alert at the Palais Brongniart Bourse building in central Paris, spokesmen said.</p>
<p>MATIF trading was switched to the GLOBEX electronic system while bond and share trading takes place on computer systems.</p>
<p>Paris is under heavy security following last week's bomb blast in an underground train which has claimed four lives.</p>
</text>
